</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Another model: ConfDiff</h2>

<div id="A7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We also applied the model on another model: ConfDiff <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite>, a model operating on <math id="A7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="SO(3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">SO(3)</annotation></semantics></math> trained on the Protein Data Bank up to December 2021.</p>
</div>
<section id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">WW Domain.</h5>

<div id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The WW domain is a small protein module that has served as a model system for studying protein folding due to its fast folding kinetics and simple topology <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>. Using ConfDiff, we computed the folding pathway from an extended to a folded conformation (Figure <a href="#A7.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ WW Domain. ‣ Appendix G Another model: ConfDiff ‣ Probing the Geometry of Diffusion Modelswith the String Method" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>). The pathway reveals progressive formation of secondary structure, consistent with experimental observations of WW domain folding <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A7.F11" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2602.22122v1/WW_domain_strng.png" id="A7.F11.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:452/76;" width="452" height="76" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 11: </span> Pathway from extended to folded conformation computed using ConfDiff. Intermediates show progressive formation of secondary structure.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.1 </span>Hyperparameters of the model</h3>

<figure id="A7.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6: </span>Hyperparameter choices for ConfDiff Model</figcaption>
<table id="A7.T6.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A7.T6.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A7.T6.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:45.5pt;padding-right:45.5pt;">     <span id="A7.T6.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hyperparameters</span></th>
